Yes, "oR will reflect the disintegration ray (and the sleep/cold).
Regardless of how you do end up attacking them (throwing daggers +
meleeing with Mjolnir when face to face is probably your best bet),
your primary goal will be to isolate the dragons so that you do not
end up surrounded by all 4 dragons at once (if surrounded, Elbereth
will be your best friend).  You can either take them to one of the 3
doorways available on the left side of Ludios, or even lure them one
by one to the magic portal to fight on the other level.  I advise
fighting them at the doorway closest to the portal so that you may
escape to the portal to heal up if necessary.  Your character should
be able to kill all of the dragons if handling them one at a time.

(P.S. if at all possible I'd try to kill the black dragon last to try
to get the disintegration resistance from the corpse, unless 1. you
have a handy dandy tinning kit 2. you already aquired the resistance,
or 3. your hunger level is already high it is not worth the risk of
choking.)

